# Easy to use, and no two people look the same

This is a homeschool desk, not a training course. A tired parent or a student should know what to do without a tour.

- Everyday words: “Add pages”, “Mark present”, “Find a book”. No SIS jargon.
- One obvious next action on each screen. Hide rare danger (delete) at the bottom.
- Big tap targets on phones. On a wide desk, let people make the whole site smaller.
- Every new page must honor `data-theme` and `data-density` tokens. Do not hard-code colors, font sizes, or spacing.
- Always ship more than one look: color themes (ascendancy, giants, academy, light, dark, contrast, forest, parchment) and densities (comfortable, cozy, compact). New chrome belongs in all of them.
- Prefer lookup and defaults (ISBN/UPC, today’s date, book + pages) over empty forms.
- If a control looks like it should change the site and does not, that is a bug.
- The desk is the Vite + React app in `web/`. FastAPI serves JSON at `/api` and the built files from `web/dist`. Print stays server HTML.
- Everyday Add patterns share one modal shell (new class, add book, add documents, new folder). Backdrop is about 75% ink.
- Themes sit immediately left of the name. The name is far right and opens Profile, Change password, and Sign out.
- Long names wrap in every density. Use `min-width: 0` and `overflow-wrap: anywhere`. Never `alert` or `confirm` — use the themed dialog.
- Class color is a real picker (swatches + any color + eyedropper). Grade weights default to Same for all (25/25/25/25).
- Documents is a folder explorer: tree, multi-select, drag to move, drop to upload. Not a stacked list.
- Attendance: the whole day cell cycles. The padlock sits top-right and does not cycle the mark.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: one frozen look -->
<section style="background:#fff; font-size:22px; padding:32px">

<!-- ✅ GOOD: tokens so every person can pick a look -->
<section class="panel">
```
